{
  "_about": "Human Rights Campaign Corporate Equality Index scores. HRC publishes no API or dataset, so these are read from the per-company pages linked in each entry's `source`. The CEI rates a COMPANY's workplace policies for its own employees -- it is not a rating of how a particular storefront treats customers. An unverified score means the company did not submit a survey that year, so the number is HRC's own assessment rather than a confirmed one.",
  "_coverage": "Only companies with storefronts a map search can actually return are listed; a packaged-goods or airline entry could never match an OpenStreetMap business name. Many large chains are absent because HRC does not rate them at all -- the index skews toward public companies, so privately held and heavily franchised chains (Chick-fil-A, In-N-Out, Trader Joe's, Aldi, Wegmans, H-E-B, Subway, Sheetz, QuikTrip, Circle K, Five Guys, Dairy Queen and others) have no CEI score to show. A business with no match here is unrated, which is not the same as scoring badly.",
  "_notInHere": "Hospitals and clinics are rated by HRC's separate Healthcare Equality Index, which scores how a facility treats LGBTQ+ PATIENTS -- including transgender-inclusive healthcare benefits -- rather than how a company treats its employees. Those scores are a different index and are not mixed in here.",
  "index": "Corporate Equality Index",
  "publisher": "Human Rights Campaign Foundation",
  "edition": 2026,
  "checkedOn": "2026-09-11",
  "maxScore": 100,
